e for us today but first  we've seen this morning the terrible  destruction caused by russian bombs to a  kiev neighborhood how are people in the  city coping with this violence and and  how are you coping  right uh so this is the shopping mall in  my area  and i could actually both hear and see  the blast last night  so um we are talking to each other to  our neighbors on on various chats and  people are just of course uh straight  away rushing to get more information  what was hit what are the consequences  what's going on uh there's no panic in  the city uh people are just making sure  that you know their close ones are safe  and if they left the houses if the  houses are intact and if the windows are  still there so i think we are at this  point quite used to these attacks and uh  the you know everybody is well  coordinated and knows what can happen  sergey i have to say i'm going to keep  this personal for a moment i think so  many viewers watch what's going on in  ukraine and they uh they look at it with  some degree of incredulity in fact  looking at you right now you as as cool  as ice how are you coping with this what  is going on with the people that allows  them to just soldier on  you can't believe how humans are  adapting to any circumstances they're  living in i mean it's it's a shock the  first days but then people get used to  sirens  people get used to uh attacks again i'm  in this neighborhood that that here's uh  the you know the shots throughout all  those three weeks so we're kind of used  to that you go to you know to do  shopping and you hear some blasts that's  that's just part of your life now you're  taking precautions but you're keeping  cool those who could not cope with that  left the city and had a right to do that  that that those who stayed we know  what's gonna happen we know that we have  to be prepared we're psychologically  stable and we're just flexible enough to  get used to that  psychologically stable okay more  questions for 